---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Felix Geelhaar — R&D ops leader, open-source author, writer on platform topology."
  lede="The long version of the bio. Third-person on this page (per the brand voice guide); first-person everywhere else."
  nav="about"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      Felix Geelhaar leads R&amp;D operations at engineering organisations where the platform
      decisions, hiring posture, and quarterly cadence already feel like a system but don't yet
      behave like one. His work focuses on the middle layer &mdash; the place where decision
      rights blur, ownership erodes, and platform debt compounds. He treats it like a product, not
      a process.
    </p>
    <p>
      He writes on the same theme: platform topology, error-budget discipline, the operating
      models that hold modern R&amp;D together, and the working agreements that keep senior
      engineers senior. His open-source work &mdash; the <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/govee-light-management">Stream Deck plugin for Govee lights</a>,
      a design system, a handful of small Go services &mdash; is small on purpose. He lives near
      Munich, speaks at engineering conferences when the room is right, and is currently focused
      on <a href={`${BASE}now`}>/now</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felixgeelhaar/">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}contact`}>Email / Cal.com</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
